Start();
register(UndefCallT);
search UndefCallT list;
define
    ucNowhere code={
        ucNoSuchName(5);
        cerr "UC-3 a statement after the refused call in the same action":;
        };
    ucEarly code={
        ucLater(1);
        cerr "UC-2b a statement after the early-bound call":;
        };
    ucFresh code={
        ucLater(1);
        };
    ;
cerr "UC-1 a call to a name defined nowhere, at the top level":;
ucTopNoSuch(3);
cerr "UC-1 next top-level statement runs":;
cerr "UC-3 the same inside an action":;
ucNowhere();
cerr "UC-3 next top-level statement runs":;
cerr "UC-2 SB-1's case: ucEarly is first built before ucLater exists":;
ucEarly();
registry(UcLater);
define
    ucLater code={ cerr "UC-2 ucLater ran":; };
    ;
search UndefCallT UcLater list;
cerr "UC-2 ucLater exists and is searched now: ucEarly still refuses, a body first built now runs it":;
ucEarly();
ucFresh();
cerr "UNDEFCALLT SENTINEL":;
stop();

undefCallT -- a call to an undefined name refuses by name (Tony, 2026-11-18, SEQ 689). Rows in genLadder/pop.sh.
It used to do nothing at all, at exit 0: runOPaccum's call arm handed an uncallable target to refuseUnknownOperator, which
speaks only for an Operators entry.
UC-1  a name defined nowhere, called at the top level: REFUSED by name; the next statement runs.
UC-2  SB-1's case (F-164): a body binds its names when first built, so ucEarly, built before ucLater exists, holds a fresh local.
      Its call refuses by name -- twice, the second time after ucLater is defined and searched -- while ucFresh, first built
      then, runs ucLater.
UC-3  the refusal ends the action, as any refusal does (2026-11-05): the statement after the call does not run, the next
      top-level statement does.
